  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1010 PM MST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nThe closed low that brought us rain showers last night is currently \nin northern Mexico and will slowly progress eastward before starting \nto lift out Sunday afternoon. Much of the area will stay dry \ntomorrow but some showery activity is expected in Hudspeth county. \nShowers will last a couple hours after sunset but will be dry \novernight. By Monday, our upper trough will be over central TX but \nlocally we will see much nicer weather featuring cooler than normal \ntemperatures, dry conditions and light winds. By midweek, a highly \namplified upper high begins to build over the area and as far north \nas Alberta and Saskatchewan. Can expect gradually warming \ntemperatures each day through Wednesday where lowland highs top out \ninto the upper 60s and low 70s. Similar highs persist through the \nremainder of the work week.",
